      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 2eb73d1fbf924bebe5874dca6095a068c2ebaea1\nparent a773e1e33b349dc819b5a0edc1c7a4839dc73b48\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792819801 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792823403 +0200\n\nhttp: reject Transfer-Encoding other than chunked\n\nA request with \"Transfer-Encoding: gzip\" or \"chunked, gzip\" is framed\nby Content-Length, or read as having no body. So is a request whose\nfirst Transfer-Encoding header is not \"chunked\". RFC 9112 section 6.3\nrequires a 400 when chunked is not the final coding. The server\nsupports no other coding.\n\nLoadBody() now accepts only a single \"chunked\", across all\nTransfer-Encoding headers. Anything else throws, which gives a 400 and\ncloses the connection. I added unit and functional tests, and updated\nthe http_request fuzz target to match.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRJ5SMZs3eEinN+Lb4iedqLwmlHIAUCatxQaxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQInnai8JpRyAXqAD7BMeQrlhL3adWT5EQEyS4\nEj9ZHialn3Kr3X3nGh9A24MBAM5LVAVnuLbZKGiapVmrENfpYrUDmbgYThCUwDkz\ngeEI\n=lghv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
