      "message": "http: reject Transfer-Encoding other than chunked\n\nA request with \"Transfer-Encoding: gzip\" or \"chunked, gzip\" is framed\nby Content-Length, or read as having no body. So is a request whose\nfirst Transfer-Encoding header is not \"chunked\". RFC 9112 section 6.3\nrequires a 400 when chunked is not the final coding. The server\nsupports no other coding.\n\nLoadBody() now accepts only a single \"chunked\", across all\nTransfer-Encoding headers. Anything else throws, which gives a 400 and\ncloses the connection. I added unit and functional tests, and updated\nthe http_request fuzz target to match.",
